{
  "_comment": [
    "Meanings for MATE workspaces, keyed by the workspace NAME with the",
    "leading order marker stripped (subscript digits, superscripts, degree",
    "sign) -- e.g. the workspace displayed as the subscript-5 aTodo2 is keyed",
    "'aTodo2'. Names without a 'meaning' have no documented purpose yet and",
    "the classifier falls back to the bare name."
  ],
  "meanings": {
    "mgmt": "Life management",
    "EXEC": "Temporary tasks",
    "C": "truck drivers license",
    "Q7": "Audi Q7",
    "PC": "managing my pc",
    "firefox": "firefox development",
    "⭐": "self health",
    "plate": "car hauler trailer",
    "aSort": "aTodo2 todo AI sorting feature",
    "dna": "learning, audiobooks, ebooks, goodreads, mtp",
    "aPrice": "aTodo2 price feature",
    ".eu+auth": "servers, Oracle, databases, proxmox",
    "⚖": "accounting, invoices, taxes. product ordering should go to: EXEC"
  },
  "rules": [
    "A workspace name of the form a<UppercaseLetter>... (aTodo2, aSort, aPrice, aChecklist, aMedia) is a subproject of the aTodo2 project.",
    "Everything belonging to the aTodo2 project goes to the aTodo2 workspace, unless a more specific aTodo2 subproject workspace fits better.",
    "The 'firefox' workspace is for FIREFOX DEVELOPMENT only (about:config, add-ons, extensions, browser internals, devtools, build/telemetry work). Ordinary web browsing, Google searches, Google Docs/Keep/Sheets and any normal website do NOT belong there -- route them to the workspace matching the page's topic, or to PC.",
    "Ignore the application name when classifying. The workspace is chosen by what the window is ABOUT, not by which app it is; a Firefox window about aTodo2 goes to aTodo2, not to 'firefox'."
  ],
  "atodo2_subproject_pattern": "^a[A-Z]",
  "catch_all": "SORT"
}
